==== ADSL Modem ====

Provided by an Infineon PSB 50601 (Amazon) ADSL chipset. This is a separate SoC with its own firmware that is configured in bridge mode with an embedded connection to the switch chip. This should appear on switch port 4 with an IP address of 192.168.5.1. Telnet and SSH to the ADSL chipset is unavailable, though there appears to be a web server and a serial port with a locked down terminal. ADSL does work by setting up a PPPoE session from within OpenWrt, but no modem statistics are available. It is suspected that there may be diagnostic webpages present in the chipset firmware that publish ADSL statistics but further analysis is required. 

==== Serial Ports ====

There are two serial ports of interest on this unit, both are populated:

  * J3 header next to the BCM4718 SoC (Where Belkin / OpenWrt would usually reside)
  * J4 header under the grey shroud covering the ADSL chipset (For ADSL firmware)

Both headers have identical pinouts.

The silkscreen indicates Pin 1 on each header:

  Pin 1 - ??
  Pin 2 - TX
  Pin 3 - RX
  Pin 4 - GND


Directions are relative from the router (I.E plug your Rx into router's Tx) \\ 

Voltage levels are 3V3, serial port settings are 8N1, 115200 bps

